{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791122163,"nonce":"Y5MmKV6K1giR/dJ6WLe9N8zvdKw=","title":"No font-variation support, so a variable face draws regular at every weight","message":"blinc_text cannot set a variable font's axes, so a variable face ignores\nthe requested weight: headings and bold text lose it. On macOS SF Pro's\nonly face is /System/Library/Fonts/SFNS.ttf, a variable font with a wght\naxis, which is why Blinc cannot adopt the real system face.\n\nThe fix is to apply the requested weight to variable faces through\nttf-parser's Face::set_variation(b\"wght\", weight), in both shaping and\nrasterizing.\n\nNote for the atlas: a weight becomes part of what a raster is, so this\ninteracts with GlyphKey. font_id already hashes the weight, so distinct\nweights key distinctly today; what changes is that they would finally\nproduce different rasters.\n\nRequested by the ashui session, tracked there as 60730bb0. It will move\nback to SF Pro once this lands.","files":null}]}